\section*{Griffiths Positivity Conjecture for Ample Vector Bundles}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
On the quadric surface, a family of rank-two ample bundles is claimed to admit no smooth strictly Griffiths-positive metric for all sufficiently large coordinatewise power pullbacks. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} On $S=\mathbb P^1\times\mathbb P^1$ let $P=\mathcal O_S(1,1)$ and let $f_m$ raise homogeneous coordinates in both factors to the $m$th power. OpenAI claims a rank-two algebraic bundle $G$ such that
\[
E_m=f_m^*G\otimes P\text{ is ample for every }m\ge1,
\]
while for every sufficiently large $m$, no smooth Hermitian metric on $E_m$ has strictly Griffiths-positive Chern curvature. Strict positivity means positive curvature in each nonzero tangent and fiber direction. The single fixed $G$ produces all members of the sequence.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 050, 2026-09-24): Compatible graph identifications use finite-order transformations for gluing but an expanding product for the obstruction. Explicit symmetric-power sections certify ampleness; a limiting positive-metric argument would produce a measure invariant under the graph transformations, contradicting the expanding dynamics.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 050, 2026-09-24): The quadric-surface rank-two bundles are ample but admit no strictly Griffiths-positive smooth Hermitian metric for sufficiently large exponents; a single such bundle disproves the universally quantified catalogue assertion.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 050, the scope page documents the following selections. The selected power-pullback family is ample in every degree but lacks a smooth strictly positive Griffiths metric beyond a threshold. The additional even-exponent very-ampleness certificate is not selected. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Its selected declaration also covers the clause used for this problem. Comparator files: QuadricBundles.lean. Declarations: OAI.QuadricCounterexample.main\_theorem.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
